DESCRIPTION Dynamic coupling: every runtime edge declared, synchronous or asynchronous (K11)
CATEGORY Dynamic Coupling
NAMESPACE EtlRSystemNS
DEFINE SYSTEM ETL-R AS etl-r-implementations-on-gcp
     DEFINE CONST MAX_RECORDS AS 200000
     DEFINE CONST RUNTIME_200K AS 7min
     # the recorded 200k flink run: 6 min 55 s. A synchronous call from produce into
     # the Target System would tie that wall-clock to the mock's availability — and
     # the mock's stale Kafka login killed load after ~34 min (docs/evidence/): entanglement

     # batch at heart: the orchestrator launches each stage job and waits for it
     DEFINE COMMUNICATION Orchestrator TO Stage Jobs AS synchronous
     # the only produce-to-load path is the topic, never a service call
     DEFINE COMMUNICATION Load TO Target System Mock AS asynchronous VIA Kafka topic target-system-target
     # confirmations flow back on their own topic; recon never reads the mock's store directly
     DEFINE COMMUNICATION Target System Mock TO Recon AS asynchronous VIA Kafka topic target-system-confirmations

# Reference data reaches enrich as a pinned contract file, not as a runtime call
DEFINE READONLYREPLICA branches AS spec/contracts/reference/branches.json
     joined at enrich; refreshed only through a contracts change

ASSERT(Communication between services adheres to the defined declarations) # [K11-1]
ASSERT(a 200k flink run completes within RUNTIME_200K, measured at 6 min 55 s) # [K11-2]
ASSERT(settle confirms exactly the written rows: targetRows confirmed == written; 200000 of 200000 in the recorded run) # [K11-3]
ASSERT(READONLYREPLICA is cached copy of reference data) # [K11-4]